@title Digital Press: Lease or Buy
@subtitle Decision for the meeting on 2026-11-12, Orchard Press commercial print shop
@author Lucinda Marsh, Owner
@date 2026-11-12

kpi Recommendation | Lease | costs $17,600 more over 4 years | neutral

The new digital press will print about 2.4 million pages a month. We compare buying and leasing over a four-year horizon.

## Options
cards
### Buy
- Purchase price: $412,000
- Service contract: $14,400 a year ($57,600 over 4 years)
- Expected resale after 4 years: $120,000
- **Net four-year cost: $349,600**
### Lease
- $7,650 a month for 48 months ($367,200)
- Service included
- Deposit: two monthly payments ($15,300)
- Optional buyout at the end: $95,000, fixed today
- **Four-year cost: $367,200**

## Four-year cost
data cost = option,usd; Buy,349600; Lease,367200
chart hbar cost unit=$ labels title="Net four-year cost"
table = Item,Buy,Lease; Upfront cash,"$412,000","$15,300 deposit"; Payments,—,"$367,200 (48 × $7,650)"; Service,"$57,600",included; Resale or buyout,"−$120,000 resale","$95,000 optional buyout"; **Net four-year cost**,"**$349,600**","**$367,200**"

## Risks
- **Buy:** ties up cash we need for the new bindery.
- **Buy:** the $120,000 resale value is a guess.
- **Lease:** locks us in for 48 months, although the buyout price is fixed today.

## Recommendation
We recommend the **lease**.
! The lease costs **$17,600 more** over four years than buying. We accept that premium because it avoids a $412,000 cash outlay and keeps cash free for the new bindery.
